  "body": "# v1.22.34 / build 2249 \u2014 Roster evidence within its actual scope\n\nPrepared roster comparisons now assess projection freshness against the league roster references used by the analysis. An unrelated unrostered catalog entry, or an explicitly stored IR/taxi/reserve asset, no longer makes an otherwise supported current finding provisional solely because its unused projection is absent or stale. The source row remains unchanged and missing values remain missing. Complete publication source clocks remain inspectable, separately from the narrower roster freshness assessment. Eligible reserves, unknown availability, legal-slot limitations, aging, failed refreshes and atomic source compatibility still qualify results.\n\nPost-trade roster evidence independently checks the resulting roster's source freshness. Moving an asset out of explicit storage does not reuse its old exclusion. No projection, actual score, optimizer, price, qualification threshold or saved preference changes. My Team and Market reuse the existing scoped prepared finding and exact-player Trade For handoff; opening it starts no search. See docs/audits/ROSTER_SOURCE_SCOPE_2249.md for the reproduced defect and live-evidence limitations.\n\n\nReleased merge: 05c717e50b47683963ed40d66946e9f6eea76694\nValidated source: 36fc76784d968fcd0917ce91821840649da1a7a4\nSource tree: c60f914d2a0b6b34c2d3e87cdce8eae4560d0b49\nAll 13 required hosted jobs and all ten canonical gates passed; 4419 canonical tests and 916 Product tests. Prior failures and resource qualifications remain in attached evidence.\n"
